   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Karsten,<p>You specified the annotation file in directory &quot;/annotation/&quot;, which is in the root directory of the system. This is very unusual in a MacOS X system since users are unallowed to create directories in system root directory. Can you please confirm that the annotation file is indeed there? <p>Cheers, <p>Yang</p></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "l6T7zQK5BwAJ",
   "from": "Yang LIAO",
   "author": "bce99ba71cd48eea",
   "date": "2018-04-09T08:20:51Z",
   "subject": "Failure to load annotation file in featureCounts",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Also, if you want use the annotation file in our packages, please specify &quot;-F SAF&quot; since our annotation files are in SAF format but not GTF.<p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vH0Ochm7BwAJ",
   "from": "Karsten Liere",
   "author": "3991ab36d2743d05",
   "date": "2018-04-09T08:59:07Z",
   "subject": "Re: Failure to load annotation file in featureCounts",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Yang,<div><br></div><div>oh, sorry, no the full path is to the annotations folder within the subread directory (<span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Monaco;font-size:10px\">/Users/karsten/Downloads/</span><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\">subread-1.6.1/annotation). And thank you, indeed, I missed the -F SAF option when using the supplied annotation file. So there must be something wrong with &quot;my&quot; gtf file. Any idea on that one?</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\">Thank you for looking into it.</font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\"><span>Cheers,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\"><span><br></span></font></div><div><font color=\"#000000\" face=\"Monaco\" size=\"1\"><span>Karsten</span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "2Bqgm5fGBwAJ",
   "from": "Karsten Liere",
   "author": "3991ab36d2743d05",
   "date": "2018-04-09T12:29:43Z",
   "subject": "Re: Failure to load annotation file in featureCounts",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">OK, here we go: change EXON to exon in the gtf file does the trick :-)<div><br></div><div>Oh dear. Thanks for listening ;-)</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div><br></div><div>Karsten</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "c1iwHluLBgAJ",
   "from": "Pham Luong Thang",
   "author": "5220f32ff751596c",
   "date": "2019-07-29T00:14:46Z",
   "subject": "Re: Failure to load annotation file in featureCounts",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Yang,<div><br></div><div>Would you please check the 1.6.5 version?</div><div>I am going to use the mm10 annotation, however, the files in the annotation folder are *txt.</div><div>I can run featureCounts with external gtf file but I prefer the in-built mm10.</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8uqeTjKNBgAJ",
   "from": "Yang LIAO",
   "author": "bce99ba71cd48eea",
   "date": "2019-07-29T00:48:30Z",
   "subject": "Re: Failure to load annotation file in featureCounts",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Pham,<div><br></div><div>Yes, the inbuilt annotations are in the SAF format, which is a textual format so the file extension is &quot;.txt&quot;.</div><div><br></div><div>You need to specify &quot;-F SAF&quot; when using these inbuilt annotation files.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Yang </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
